n_text": "Use formal singular agreement for the group as one unit, in the present: A group of tourists ____ outside.", "explanation": "For the explicitly requested singular unit and present time, a group is takes is. Notional plural agreement is possible in other contexts.", "options": ["be", "were", "are", "is"], "correct_answer": "is"}, "reason": "BRITISH_COLLECTIVE_AGREEMENT"}, {"n": 414, "original_id": "0ce600f8-ac73-ee18-e7d0-06b539fc9a10", "original_hash": "b5f9954e94370e324d5c137646ef1fb83393abffad0ac631708f9559f4b610f7", "replacement_id": "23ce58a4-7ba8-5362-ae9f-23ceba6cec32", "patch": {"question_text": "Use an indefinite article for an unspecified singular item or person, not something already identified. France is _____ European country.", "explanation": "Use a before a consonant sound and an before a vowel sound. European and university begin with a /j/ consonant sound; hour begins with a vowel sound.", "options": ["a", "an", "the", "no article"], "correct_answer": "a"}, "reason": "ARTICLE_REFERENCE_UNDERSPECIFIED"}, {"n": 415, "original_id": "2bf04164-f874-764a-cb3d-3f81b99ba6f6", "original_hash": "87b6d0879cd70c7a3fd56081c7868da7e57f47e1d4443f501654d5779abb9110", "replacement_id": "6ae1924a-7a98-5841-8d6d-cfca545c3edd", "patch": {"question_text": "Use an indefinite article for an unspecified singular item or person, not something already identified. She ate _____ apple after lunch.", "explanation": "Use a before a consonant sound and an before a vowel sound. European and university begin with a /j/ consonant sound; hour begins with a vowel sound.", "options": ["an", "a", "the", "no article"], "correct_answer": "an"}, "reason": "ARTICLE_REFERENCE_UNDERSPECIFIED"}, {"n": 416, "original_id": "8a78c95c-3586-5619-30ec-704115f6a059", "original_hash": "cf9af025b8007e3bbd27ec0f046649f1fe76c03cfc858fe3c240ba6479e7c32f", "replacement_id": "10357120-a98d-5129-822e-e097b1eb1af3", "patch": {"question_text": "Use an indefinite article for an unspecified singular ite