appy → ____ (superlative).", "explanation": "The task asks for the single-word comparison form, including the correct spelling change. A form with more/most may occur in other contexts.", "options": ["happiest", "most happy", "happyest", "more happy"], "correct_answer": "happiest"}, "reason": "ACCEPTABLE_COMPARATIVE_VARIANT"}, {"n": 455, "original_id": "8a11b686-fa80-453e-b6a3-211fe6d71fb5", "original_hash": "e2811e2a09317097dffe6b0da08e7c9ae132850c76a842f152088dbffb161145", "replacement_id": "711a95b2-0656-50d7-9bbf-488b28f3d83d", "patch": {"question_text": "Use the single-word form with the -er or -est ending. Choose the correct comparative: This explanation is ____ than the last one.", "explanation": "The task asks for the single-word comparison form, including the correct spelling change. A form with more/most may occur in other contexts.", "options": ["the more clearer", "clearer", "clearest", "more clear"], "correct_answer": "clearer"}, "reason": "ACCEPTABLE_COMPARATIVE_VARIANT"}, {"n": 508, "original_id": "f3e05fe9-deea-4154-bd29-78d64cbf5b93", "original_hash": "622d5aebdabe993a8cd8207e9f4bf14ed92e154fcbcb5fb0c9c6e8d548dfc2a0", "replacement_id": "e5085e9c-c5f3-5a88-a10e-8e9696497338", "patch": {"question_text": "Choose the sentence using the single-word comparative form of clear.", "explanation": "Clearer is the single-word comparative of clear. More clear can be acceptable, but it is not the form requested.", "options": ["This explanation is clearer than the last one.", "This explanation is more clear than the last one.", "This explanation is clearest than the last one.", "This explanation is the more clearer."], "correct_answer": "This explanation is clearer than the last one."}, "reason": "MULTIPLE_VALID_ANSWERS"}, {"n": 513, "original_id": "0012ad81-0fe5-4537-a8f1-e0157b3eaee8", "original_hash": "31c3cb4f21ac27f720987a9a235b191262611ea7278f53996eb073d2b8dad646", "replacement_id": "21fa48f3-e58f-58c0-9b12-6beb72f590c1", "patch": {"explanation": "Cost-effective is a correctly hyphenated compound adjective before solution.", "options": ["risk-taking-mentality", "cost-effective solution", "wide-spread-opinion", "heavy-loaded vehicle"], "correct_answer": "cost-effective solution"}, "reason": "EXPLANATION_OR_ACCESSIBILITY_CLEANUP"}, {"n": 514, "original_id": "08bd9187-2fd5-4b26-8ff9-d44eea69a573", "original_hash": "a247bc7870c0b915be6b91ca1a205827b918f76b5d0d96d563f6d9e41e869a63", "replacement_id": "c3149693-768c-5c19-bdf1-69763fb72709", "patch": {"explanation": "World-renowned joins two words that modify expert; the hyphen keeps the modifier together.", "options": ["He’s a world-renowned expert in fungal biology.", "She wrote a last minute-speech for the ceremony.", "They met during a five-years-old reunion event.", "This is a purely evidence-basedapproach."], "correct_answer": "He’s a world-renowned expert in fungal biology."}, "reason": "EXPLANATION_OR_ACCESSIBILITY_CLEANUP"}, {"n": 515, "original_id": "1294e3d3-2a7a-42c1-91e1-ba7b9dbac124", "original_hash": "1f31b77fe269415f35bcbba076ed509779e000d5f80aeee39ff0294d80cdc505", "replacement_id": "60f056fe-8347-54b9-8f46-a286e2ccdaed", "patch": {"explanation": "An -ly adverb such as widely is normally not joined to its following participle with a hyphen: widely spread.", "options": ["A fast-paced drama series.", "A far-reaching decision.", "A deep-rooted belief.", "A widely-spread rumor."], "correct_answer": "A widely-spread rumor."}, "reason": "EXPLANATION_OR_ACCESSIBILITY_CLEANUP"}, {"n": 517, "original_id": "37fedfc0-acdc-4cae-9851-42bf3c13e2ca", "original_hash": "d0b2a17d9a45ee026d630edd0c2eb03ad3367c939a4cf287383d6d6b9f8291bc", "replacement_id": "2da461c2-c169-5bc2-9f31-741fd7c24bc2", "patch": {"explanation": "Hand-made correctly describes boots made by hand; the other choices contain malformed modifiers.", "options": ["The movie was a two hours-long experience.", "She bought a pair of hand-made leather boots.", "The class discussed a well writing-structured essay.", 