gular subject and were with a plural subject.", "options": ["was", "were", "is", "are"], "correct_answer": "was"}, "reason": "TENSE_UNDERSPECIFIED"}, {"n": 1545, "original_id": "c308c624-5b36-3993-e66c-1ae56034fd3d", "original_hash": "34f912d2cc819b6ee01c8f2ec2a2574f8bfddfd5f6d9f5f13c3920c49e6ea87d", "replacement_id": "a6b28739-a29a-5055-b01b-97b4f8a8550b", "patch": {"question_text": "Complete the sentence about yesterday: They _____ tired after the long walk.", "explanation": "The time is explicitly in the past. Use was with a singular subject and were with a plural subject.", "options": ["were", "was", "are", "is"], "correct_answer": "were"}, "reason": "TENSE_UNDERSPECIFIED"}, {"n": 1546, "original_id": "d078a8bb-b9bd-79ad-004b-5e872ea3f714", "original_hash": "bb682ef85e37b1360aa109b2ac8e4b7e1501112d04467ef6c775deda1cdcfc8d", "replacement_id": "d8d94f37-8761-58c4-8b19-ba5ae4cd9779", "patch": {"question_text": "Complete the sentence about yesterday: We _____ at the sports centre on Saturday.", "explanation": "The time is explicitly in the past. Use was with a singular subject and were with a plural subject.", "options": ["were", "was", "are", "is"], "correct_answer": "were"}, "reason": "TENSE_UNDERSPECIFIED"}, {"n": 1547, "original_id": "fb2b94b3-961f-c0f4-4a5e-a513a306cb22", "original_hash": "2400f31184928193b362ac951d599c7bc087f1e4e45c917bd81a379e708804e4", "replacement_id": "268b6cdf-b706-5faf-8e89-62ec13a6f1d6", "patch": {"question_text": "Complete the sentence about yesterday: The children _____ in the playground at lunchtime.", "explanation": "The time is explicitly in the past. Use was with a singular subject and were with a plural subject.", "options": ["were", "was", "are", "is"], "correct_answer": "were"}, "reason": "TENSE_UNDERSPECIFIED"}, {"n": 1665, "original_id": "04311494-df9b-767e-2bf6-c948abd786ff", "original_hash": "49488f445ab1f085bba8e16b71c668b970dafe615e06eae471df9f1b0c31078e", "replacement_id": "a651332f-8962-5cb2-a61a-c8fe72436cee", "patch": {"image_url": "https://www.brainsheist.com/question-assets/2026-10-12/audit-1665.bc9e960366bd.svg", "explanation": "P lies between the 200 m and 250 m contours, so about 225 m is reasonable.", "image_alt_text": "A contour map has lines labelled 100, 150, 200 and 250 metres. Point P is clearly marked between two neighbouring contours."}, "reason": "CONTOUR_POINT_OVERLAP"}, {"n": 1735, "original_id": "eb2757aa-b950-471e-5351-f977ed5c2352", "original_hash": "f804e034676987bccf29283d17f38046954f7a6b15d3b53a500b6b4c18d176b3", "replacement_id": "c8cedab3-1917-50b4-8427-2aa5878c9a08", "patch": {"question_text": "Most of Earth’s fresh water is stored in which reservoir?", "explanation": "Most fresh water is stored as ice in glaciers and ice sheets. This self-contained question does not require a missing diagram.", "options": ["A small pond", "One cloud", "A drinking cup", "Ice and glaciers"], "correct_answer": "Ice and glaciers"}, "reason": "MISSING_VISUAL_STIMULUS"}, {"n": 1750, "original_id": "2b4a32a2-b793-44b7-ac8e-1ee1deb2fda5", "original_hash": "2a2de890a241487a602bdf7d1c1950418c58dbe4f285d27a3b832ce8c44dcd40", "replacement_id": "12c550e0-7ac9-5e35-af5d-5c1778a9d428", "patch": {"question_text": "What is the German noun meaning school?", "options": ["Schel", "Schoole", "Schul", "Schule"], "correct_answer": "Schule", "explanation": "The German noun is Schule. German nouns start with a capital letter."}, "reason": "GERMAN_CAPITALISATION_AND_FORM"}, {"n": 1751, "original_id": "2ce16146-4baa-46cb-9029-5fce1c1bb23b", "original_hash": "1eceae8107930f6e12d17121aea1814e9eb119f19c5c35fbb58f025ace721518", "replacement_id": "8c8672db-7b50-59dc-b987-0876f9be00b7", "patch": {"question_text": "Complete the German translation of they eat: Sie ____.", "options": ["isst", "esse", "essen", "esst"], "correct_answer": "essen", "explanation": "The third-person plural sie takes essen in the present tense."}, "reason": "GERMAN_CAPITALISATION_AND_FORM"}, {"n": 1752, "original_id": "2fde555f-9a7e-478e-9236-f75463260a9a", "original_hash": "a5db9a193afbf6981d3e5583700cb9987b7895a24e89be8bd1a75902ea8db440", "replacement_id": "5d595b97-9570-5b9c-ba68-397c627b0e8f", "patch": {"explanation": "Tisch is masculine; its nominative singular definite article is der.", "options": ["Der", "Die", "Das", "Den"], "correct_answer": "Der"}, "reason": "EXPLANATION_OR_ACCESSIBILITY_CLEANUP"}, {"n": 1753, "original_id": "521d7786-9de9-4200-ab65-5bdde53a85ae", "original_hash": "31fd6498cb18b00423ed19b00325025818a224d207b2860d5d07fbb85c6a781a", "replacement_id": "e4ee8d71-351b-5387-ae97-08446385fd01", "patch": {"explanation": "Motion into the cinema uses in + das, contracted to ins.", "options": ["Ich gehe in Kino.", "Ich gehe im Kino", "Ich gehe ins Kino", "Ich gehe zu Kino."], "correct_answer": "Ich gehe ins Kino"}, "reason": "EXPLANATION_OR_ACCESSIBILITY_CLEANUP"}, {"n": 1756, "original_id": "60e249a6-d34f-500e-392e-1b92fb8f940c", "original_hash": "b32acb95d17ae06f4cdbfbcf03b7aa894348a814493bf42cf76ec148a4a36dc0", "replacement_id": "bb96bc8d-5dd6-5b88-94ac-d601a9a588b8", "patch": {"question_text": "Which sentence means I live in Berlin, not near Berlin?", "explanation": "In Berlin means inside the city. Bei Berlin can be grammatical but means near Berlin.", "options": ["Ich wohne im Berlin.", "Ich wohne auf Berlin.", "Ich wohne bei Berlin.", "Ich wohne in Berlin."], "correct_answer": "Ich wohne in Berlin."}, "reason": "MULTIPLE_VALID_ANSWERS"}, {"n": 1759, "original_id": "7d22bc5a-13ec-456b-bdf4-bb0489f6df33", "original_hash": "a472ad22f6df7c0561b2435dfd4ceff8a1e1e1bf06b1f076693c56c3d261d633", "replacement_id": "ce03e1be-b8f8-5c48-82bb-a4580e8a5549", "patch": {"explanation": "Apfel is masculine, so its nominative singular definite article is der.", "options": ["Der", "Die", "Das", "Den"], "correct_answer": "Der"}, "reason": "EXPLANATION_OR_ACCESSIBILITY_CLEANUP"}, {"n": 1764, "original_id": "ac9791fa-2527-42fb-af06-4818ae113448", "original_hash": "5b2aaa473c933230f242ace294c9fa62dda0593c7d5eda30713c5a3f5a3031a2", "replacement_id": "1ee8f55b-0acd-58db-913f-ba79d8f4d625", "patch": {"explanation": "Das Gehirn controls thought; es denkt means it thinks.", "options": ["Es denkt 🧠", "Es läuft 🏃‍♂️", "Es isst 🍽️", "Es kochen"], "correct_answer": "Es denkt 🧠"}, "reason": "EXPLANATION_OR_ACCESSIBILITY_CLEANUP"}, {"n": 1766, "original_id": "c09fa4ab-b77f-40c7-9d9a-73d7e0750b9e", "original_hash": "2a521d4547c5072e3748d740714c4bff16c7af3c8a3e4b80c25fbceb7789489c", "replacement_id": "ac01e0bb-980f-5240-8a8a-8d902b32778e", "patch": {"explanation": "Mädchen is grammatically neuter, so its singular nominative article is das.", "options": ["der", "Die", "Das", "Den"], "correct_answer": "Das"}, "reason": "EXPLANATION_OR_ACCESSIBILITY_CLEANUP"}, {"n": 1769, "original_id": "d1e634bc-a624-4f39-b659-49789127e02b", "original_hash": "2cd1cea781c72ffb6b1f5b2498bb7a0ecd18f675b61e3608eaab9680e9a12a60", "replacement_id": "c5536a30-2d00-50ec-be25-705f83c7bf39", "patch": {"correct_answer": "gehe", "explanation": "After Morgen, the finite verb takes second position: Morgen gehe ich ins Kino. The subject ich is already present in the stem.", "options": ["ich gehe", "gehe", "gehe ich", "ins Kino gehe ich"]}, "reason": "KEY_DUPLICATES_SUBJECT"}, {"n": 1804, "original_id": "c74be83b-7d6d-41dc-901a-3dfb01e2c2eb", "original_hash": "02a553eeb1be43364807ace7ccebfa722968e222c57c348816d61f7a059f4476", "replacement_id": "3ba6016a-c48e-5f58-814f-d5464f0e6bd8", "patch": {"question_text": "Which example is primary data collected directly for your own research?", "options": ["a textbook summary", "an interview you conduct for the research", "a review article", "a published summary of someone else’s survey"], "correct_answer": "an interview you conduct for the research", "explanation": "An interview conducted for your own research collects data directly. The other sources summarize previously collected information."}, "reason": "PRIMARY_DATA_CONTEXT"}, {"n": 1843, "original_id": "35c1ad18-4d7e-4547-b310-d8517c3b0994", "original_hash": "81b0bbc4f76fcdbdcb5426f079faf611613044847939684a2da507d186618cfb", "replacement_id": "9d1e6437-f16f-5c7e-bfe8-09dab486d340", "patch": {"question_text": "Which storage device is designed to plug directly into a USB port without a separate drive or cable?", "explanation": "A USB flash drive plugs directly into a USB port. Other storage devices can be portable but do not match this specific description.", "options": ["SSD", "CD/DVD", "USB flash drive", "HDD"], "correct_answer": "USB flash drive"}, "reason": "MULTIPLE_PORTABLE_MEDIA"}, {"n": 1947, "original_id": "0f08b22c-1272-21f6-db12-dfa54a613e69", "original_hash": "661198552e8ce48b41155e400933d34fe42576cff1f11297e493c8139a51313d", "replacement_id": "2626a804-9d15-5138-a72f-de2b5cd0f224", "patch": {"image_url": "https://www.brainsheist.com/question-assets/2026-10-12/audit-1947.d0bd64b44312.svg", "explanation": "Folding on Line B would make the two halves match exactly.", "image_alt_text": "An asymmetric kite has four candidate dashed lines labelled A, B, C and D. Reflect the shape across each line to test its symmetry."}, "reason": "MULTIPLE_SYMMETRY_LINES"}, {"n": 1960, "original_id": "e8149760-3c67-9433-1a66-639a26af1f32", "original_hash": "de33e63211db5f2bb4ebdd147bcfedea366a9bb294036a28fb0f76fb61d916f0", "replacement_id": "5d8dc49f-e49f-5ed8-923f-670ca1f83bf3", "patch": {"image_url": "https://www.brainsheist.com/question-assets/2026-10-12/audit-1960.c7061cbbe3bc.svg", "explanation": "Angle C has a square corner and measures 90 degrees.", "image_alt_text": "Four angle cards labelled A, B, C and D show openings. Card C has a small square marker; card D shows a horizontal line and a semicircular angle arc."}, "reason": "ANGLE_MARKING_AMBIGUOUS"}, {"n": 2035, "original_id": "1a7dc78f-1735-4f2f-9ce3-8569cdc69d65", "original_hash": "d9bcf0e0155ff88b31d33f19416a42dde0d7d83e5db76268478f6308bc186a1c", "replacement_id": "45182fb1-f22e-5684-82c3-d8984524fba6", "patch": {"question_text": "Multiply and give the product in simplest form: 3/4 × 2/3.", "explanation": "3/4 × 2/3 = 6/12, which simplifies to 1/2. The task explicitly requests simplest form.", "options": ["6/12", "1/2", "3/7", "2/7"], "correct_answer": "1/2"}, "reason": "EQUIVALENT_CORRECT_OPTIONS"}, {"n": 2079, "original_id": "8d2035b0-d973-45a8-ab7a-a75d7959f65d", "original_hash": "d494f3fa68d3298cf72c05300b22d0534a7b3a0fad02620490ec8d7b07e4638b", "replacement_id": "b110485b-a493-5f03-8987-7f5e2384a915", "patch": {"explanation": "The diagram shows a square with four equal sides and right angles.", "options": ["square", "circle", "triangle", "line"], "correct_answer": "square", "image_alt_text": "A closed four-sided shape with equal horizontal and vertical sides is drawn."}, "reason": "EXPLANATION_OR_ACCESSIBILITY_CLEANUP"}, {"n": 2081, "original_id": "faeb9460-220d-44e9-8117-0f37b42d3891", "original_hash": "495bc4e618596cac8244f5b9e4cee6a181c277dbfa68eccfa414d44a4f9931e1", "replacement_id": "365b922b-4756-5c0b-b9d1-fc1ba1a905a3", "patch": {"question_text": "What is the measure, in degrees, of the angle marked with a small square?", "correct_answer": "90", "options": ["90", "95", "100", "180"], "explanation": "The small square marks a right angle, whose measure is 90 degrees.", "image_alt_text": "A triangle has a small square marking one angle at the lower-left vertex."}, "reason": "WRONG_ANGLE_KEY"}, {"n": 2265, "original_id": "0e202bef-4047-1d48-c25c-ffed67dac8a3", "original_hash": "5a361b3aa5394f47ea4631ac0099f211e7724c05697267cd717e5923bcd5519b", "replacement_id": "870c71e6-fb2b-5b82-8e4f-bbeea874d4f8", "patch": {"image_url": "https://www.brainsheist.com/question-assets/2026-10-12/audit-2265.a5a187bca353.svg", "explanation": "Grasshoppers transfer energy to frogs, so fewer grasshoppers mean less food is immediately available to frogs."}, "reason": "INCOMPLETE_FOOD_CHAIN_DIAGRAM"}, {"n": 2279, "original_id": "6844d924-22ee-b4dd-1f0b-ca45f8144b06", "original_hash": "bc